WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.567
Dropout.

2
00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:06.367
To stop a network memorizing, we randomly switch parts of it off while it trains.

3
00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:14.733
During training, each neuron's output is zeroed with probability p, commonly between point one and point five.

4
00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:17.500
And the random mask is fresh for every batch.

5
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.333
Here's a network mid-training.

6
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:22.167
Some hidden units vanish.

7
00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:29.833
Because no neuron can count on any other, knowledge spreads across redundant pathways instead of brittle co-adapted circuits.

8
00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:32.667
There are two ways to think about it.

9
00:00:32.967 --> 00:00:37.300
In training, every mask is a different sub-network, and they all share weights.

10
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.267
PyTorch scales the survivors up, so the expected magnitude matches inference.

11
00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:46.300
At inference, dropout turns off, giving you their implicit average.

12
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.033
Forget eval, and predictions turn noisy.

13
00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:51.333
And what it buys you.

14
00:00:51.633 --> 00:00:57.469
Before dropout, training accuracy is ninety nine percent but validation is only eighty two.

15
00:00:57.469 --> 00:00:58.624
That's memorizing.

16
00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:02.600
After, they sit at ninety three and ninety, so it generalizes.

17
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.467
It's one layer in PyTorch.

18
00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:09.133
Dropout with point five, right after the first hidden layer.

19
00:01:09.433 --> 00:01:11.233
And a lighter point three deeper in.

20
00:01:11.533 --> 00:01:13.317
Then eval before predicting.

21
00:01:13.317 --> 00:01:15.100
Never predict in train mode.

22
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.533
Here's a real case.

23
00:01:17.833 --> 00:01:23.000
You have only a few hundred confirmed transits, and your dense head can memorize all of them.

24
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.767
It does: ninety nine percent train, eighty two validation.

25
00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.504
Dropout at point five closes the gap.

26
00:01:29.504 --> 00:01:35.500
A bonus: keep it on at inference and predict thirty times for a cheap uncertainty estimate.

27
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:37.500
Let's recap.

28
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.567
Dropout zeroes random neurons during training.

29
00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.733
That forces redundant pathways.

30
00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:45.500
Think of it as an ensemble of sub-networks.

31
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.427
And turn it off with eval.

32
00:01:47.427 --> 00:01:49.367
Next up: weight initialization.
